.TH IMGVIEW 1 "" "imgview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imgview, iv \- image viewer for close inspection of pixels and metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imgview
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ...]
.br
.B iv
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imgview
shows an image scaled to the window. When zoomed in it shows the stored
pixel values unmodified (nearest neighbour) by default, and it can invert
colors and adjust gamma and saturation to make faint features easier to
spot. An info panel shows the file size, dimensions and EXIF, XMP and IPTC metadata.
.PP
.I path
may be an image file or a folder; for a folder, its first image is opened.
The left and right arrow keys then step through the folder's images. With
several paths, they step through just those images, in the order given (a
folder among them contributes its images; missing and unreadable files are
skipped). Without a path, a file picker opens.
.B iv
is a short alias for
.BR imgview .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B + = \-
Zoom in, zoom out (the mouse wheel zooms around the pointer).
.TP
.B 0
Fit the image to the window.
.TP
.B r
Zoom to exactly 1:1, centred on the pointer.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Pan a zoomed image (with Shift: by one image pixel). Left and right switch
to the previous and next image in the folder when the whole image fits in
the view; when it only fits sideways, they do nothing.
.TP
.B i
Cycle zoom-in resampling: nearest (true pixels), bicubic, Lanczos3.
.TP
.B n
Toggle color inversion.
.TP
.B . , /
Gamma up (darker), gamma down (brighter), reset gamma.
.TP
.B ; l \(aq
Saturation up (more vivid; doubles every 4 presses, up to 1600%),
saturation down (by 10%, down to grey), reset saturation to 100%.
.TP
.B Backspace
Reset inversion, gamma and saturation.
.TP
.B ?
Show or hide the help panel, which lists every key and the current view
settings. Keys keep working while it is open.
.TP
.B m
Show or hide the info panel.
.TP
.B o
Open an image with a file picker.
.TP
.B s
Save the image area as shown (zoom, inversion, gamma and saturation
applied) as a PNG next to the image, or in the Pictures folder if that isn't writable. With
Shift: choose where to save.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the help panel, or leave fullscreen, or quit.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/JCallicoat/imgview
